Description: Both monitors in 3D at once share the declaration library
 Each monitor's 3D area set up libstereo-declare on its own event queue, but the
 library is set up once in a process: stereo_declare_wayland_init() answers -EBUSY
 to a second call. With 3D on by default in both monitors (patch 0009), opening a
 3D clip in the clip monitor while the project monitor showed one in 3D made the
 second monitor say "the stereo declaration library could not start" and show the
 packed frame. The library is now set up once, on an event queue of its own, for
 every 3D area of the process, and ended by the last one; each area declares its
 own surface.
